course: dictionary
lesson: 15185
title: Seasonally
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Seasonally is an adverb made from season, and the -ly ending tells you how something happens. It means in a way that depends on or changes with the seasons of the year.
explain: «Strawberries are sold seasonally, so you find them in the shops mostly in summer.» The clue is the season: the time of year decides when strawberries are on sale.
explain: It can also mean only at certain seasons. «The beach café is open seasonally, so it is shut in winter.» The café is open in some seasons and closed in others.
explain: Look for season words around it: spring, summer, autumn, winter. If the season decides when something happens, seasonally is probably the word you need.
fact: Season means one of the four parts of the year: spring, summer, autumn and winter.
fact: «Seasonally» means in a way that depends on the seasons, or at certain seasons only.
fact: Animals can migrate seasonally, moving to new places at certain times of year.
fact: «Seasonally adjusted» means figures have been changed to remove the effect of the seasons, so they can be compared fairly.
fact: A good check is to put your meaning into the sentence: if «at certain times of year» still makes sense, you have it right.
exercise: «Strawberries are sold seasonally, so you find them in the shops mostly in summer.» What does seasonally mean here? | Every single day of the year | Very quickly | *Depending on the seasons, so only at certain times of year | Without any cost
exercise: Birds migrate seasonally, flying south when winter comes. What does seasonally tell you? | The birds never move at all | *The flights depend on the time of year | The birds fly only at night | The birds are very tired
exercise: Find the word that tells you the change depends on the time of year: «The ice cream van runs seasonally, from spring to autumn.» | ice | autumn | *seasonally | van
test: «The farm sells apples seasonally.» What does this mean? | Apples are sold for free | Apples are sold only by weight | *Apples are sold at certain times of the year | Apples are sold in every shop, all year round
test: «The beach café is open seasonally, so it is shut in winter.» Why is the café shut in winter? | Because it has no food to sell | Because the owner is on holiday for ever | *Because it only opens at certain times of year | Because it is too sunny
exam: Maya says seasonally means every day. Is she right? | Yes, because seasons happen every day | Yes, it means every day, all year long | No, it means very fast | *No, it means depending on the seasons, or only at certain seasons
